    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0091" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1508: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-25T14:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.41
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>54. Your January 24, 1 p.m. Reply of President to your January 15, 6 p.m. which
                    was presented before my arrival, is in pouch on way to Washington.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d5-f1"/> Since arriving the President has informed me that he
                    notified leaders of his party some time ago when insisting on necessity of
                    election reform that he would resign before participating as President in
                    elections of character of last one.</p>
                <pb facs="0092" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/>
                <p>I wish the Department had given me time to present the matter in my own way and
                    in the spirit indicated in the conference held in the State Department on the
                    afternoon of January 10th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
